The rectangular plot measures approximately 12 metres across its northern frontage and 20 metres deep, adjoining a private road and public-road connection. SAM reports orange planning zoning and commercial surroundings.

Registered acquisitions are three four-storey shophouses: 88/24 on deed 167704, 88/25 on deed 167705 and 88/26 on deed 167722. The survey instead describes three storeys, a mezzanine and a roof-level addition, with all three units internally connected. Verify registration, plans, permits and actual floor configuration.

Material source disclosure: the open-sided covered extension at the front encroaches on the road boundary. Confirm boundaries, permits, corrective or removal obligations and related costs with SAM and the responsible authority before purchase.

The frontage road is private. SAM states that an easement has been registered for the property plots. It connects to the Chon Buri bypass (Highway 361) and has an approximately eight-metre concrete carriageway. Verify the easement instrument, extent, rights and actual access; the frontage road is not represented as public.

From Sukhumvit Road (Highway 3), take Suk Prayun Road (Highway 315) toward Phanat Nikhom, passing Chalerm Thai, Nawamin Rachini Camp, Wat Thammanimit and the 21st Infantry Regiment. Turn left onto the Chon Buri bypass (Highway 361) for approximately 620 metres; the property is on the left. SAM lists an artillery battalion nearby.

SAM showed direct-purchase status and this price on 11 September 2026. Contact 02-686-1888, sales@sam.or.th or LINE @samline, quoting 3A2042, to confirm availability, price, viewing, access rights and terms.

